    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="1053" n="1043" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1043"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thomas B. McCabe to
                        Mr. John K. Howard, at Manila</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-22">22 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92224. Please pass to General Marshall. Reference Part 2, 917 dated 16 June
                    signed by Marshall, Howard, Vogelback and Johnson. We have conferred with Army,
                    Navy and OWMR<anchor n="27" xml:id="d770-f1"/> and have every reason to believe
                    that the program for returning to United States new and serviceable items by the
                    services will be discontinued. OWMR will call meeting probably Monday to be
                    attended by Army, Navy, CPA<anchor n="28" xml:id="d770-f2"/> and ourselves to
                    make final decision and my informal talks with agencies concerned indicate that
                    your request will be acted upon favorably. The directive to be issued by the
                    services may limit the discontinuance of shipments for a period of 30 days
                    during which time the prospects of consummating the China deal can be
                    determined.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
